  "spec": "Track D, the hint probe on the FROZEN model (first step of the \"feed it search\" idea of tips/core/v2: SYMBIONT's hint compiler, tested on our own model without any training). Same ten contexts as ledger lines 25 to 36, fresh rows. Columns: init = the frozen 23.7M checkpoint (fleet_M_x2 valley_002, in-corpus lineage), random slots, four views, as in every earlier read; inith = the SAME frozen checkpoint with three label-derived hint columns appended to its input (a ridge, a 16-nearest-neighbour target mean and a small boosted-tree model; SEARCH rows get each hint out of fold on the bank's five folds, so no row's hint saw its own label; fresh rows get the mean of the five fold models); hridge, hknn, hgbm = each hint alone as a predictor (the fold-model mean on fresh rows). Baseline init_mean3. Only the fresh-row predictions are scored; the SEARCH-row column of a hinted block is not out of fold as a whole and is never stacked. Registered before any hinted column exists (the builder option is not yet staged). READING RULE, fixed now, over the ten contexts: (U) the model USES hints if inith beats init on at least 7 of 10 with a positive family-mean difference; (A) the model ADDS to its hints if inith also beats the best of its three hints on that context on at least 6 of 10. U and A: hints are worth feeding to our model as it is, and worth training for. U without A: the frozen model is a copier of its best hint, so hint-conditioned training (with corrupted hints and a beat-your-hint loss) is needed before hints can pay at stack level, where the same classic columns already sit. Not U: the model ignores columns it was never trained on, and the hint route needs training before it can be judged. Prediction: U holds (7 or more of 10, mean gain between +0.2 and +0.8 u, the largest on 769243ee where a ridge is far above the frozen model); A fails (inith beats its best hint on 4 or fewer of 10). Descriptive: ten contexts, one seed, in-corpus init; at 7 of 10 the chance under a fair coin is about 0.17, so U and A are direction calls, not tests.",
